reward or not for this choice.

00:04:04.746 --> 00:04:08.330
You see that the animal learns to
pick green when green is good,

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:11.485
and orange when orange is good, etc.

00:04:11.486 --> 00:04:13.370
So, this is the kind of

00:04:13.371 --> 00:04:16.600
reinforcement learning
behavior we look at.

00:04:16.601 --> 00:04:19.455
What's interesting here is that,

00:04:19.456 --> 00:04:24.015
if you plot the aggregated behavior.

00:04:24.016 --> 00:04:26.520
So here, it's the dotted line,

00:04:26.521 --> 00:04:30.410
I plotted the probability of
choosing either of the bandits.

00:04:30.411 --> 00:04:33.335
This can be really
captured super well

00:04:33.336 --> 00:04:36.485
by the simple kind of
algorithm we saw before.

00:04:36.486 --> 00:04:40.590
So, this is where
the algorithm is coming from.

00:04:40.591 --> 00:04:44.790
Computer science have been
helpful in capturing behavior.

00:04:44.791 --> 00:04:47.960
So, here we have the action
value for both of the bandits,

00:04:47.961 --> 00:04:50.795
