00:05:46.451 --> 00:05:51.110
What you see here is
an animal getting a reward

00:05:51.111 --> 00:05:55.325
and you see that those dopamine
neurons increased the spiking.

00:05:55.326 --> 00:05:57.590
So, they seemed to be signaling, "Oh,

00:05:57.591 --> 00:06:01.225
something better than I was
expecting happened here."

00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:05.010
After a while, the animal
learns to predict this reward.

00:06:05.011 --> 00:06:08.280
So, that's we can think
of Pavlov's experiment,

00:06:08.281 --> 00:06:10.425
the bell predicts the food,

00:06:10.426 --> 00:06:12.540
so that's what CS here means.

00:06:12.541 --> 00:06:16.460
When you get that, this is where
you get dopamine signaling.

00:06:16.461 --> 00:06:18.780
So, that's a positive
reward prediction error.

00:06:18.781 --> 00:06:20.040
Then, when you get the reward,

00:06:20.041 --> 00:06:23.985
you're expecting it, and
there's no dopamine signaling.

00:06:23.986 --> 00:06:27.230
Then, when the animal was expecting
a reward but did not get it,

00:06:27.231 --> 00:06:28.940
there's a deep in signal.

00:06:28.941 --> 00:06:31.805
So, this set of neurons seems to be

00:06:31.806 --> 00:06:33.680
encoding something exactly what

00:06:33.681 --> 00:06:35.875
you would want for a
reward prediction.

00:06:35.876 --> 00:06:38.670
People have gone further,
looked at the circuits,

00:06:38.671 --> 00:06:41.505
seen who dopamine neurons talk to,

00:06:41.506 --> 00:06:43.220
and essentially what
