00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:15.910
Okay, so I've given you

00:20:15.911 --> 00:20:19.180
the intuition already but I'm
going to make it more precise.

00:20:19.181 --> 00:20:22.360
If you remember when you
were learning how to drive,

00:20:22.361 --> 00:20:25.390
you were given a lot of
instructions that you,

00:20:25.391 --> 00:20:27.190
if you're a careful student, well,

00:20:27.191 --> 00:20:29.770
try to actively keep in
mind at the beginnings.

00:20:29.771 --> 00:20:31.990
So, for example, the speed limits,

00:20:31.991 --> 00:20:35.125
remembering to signal when turning.

00:20:35.126 --> 00:20:37.420
Remembering more obstruct things like

00:20:37.421 --> 00:20:39.850
the rules for how to
handle a four-way stop,

00:20:39.851 --> 00:20:42.610
or a red light in the US,

00:20:42.611 --> 00:20:45.430
and also even more
obstruct things like

00:20:45.431 --> 00:20:48.025
how to not kill bicyclists.

00:20:48.026 --> 00:20:55.300
Okay. So, you'll try to very
actively remember this.

00:20:55.301 --> 00:20:57.460
You will keep this in
your mind, so like,

00:20:57.461 --> 00:21:00.670
okay, I need to not
go faster than 25.

00:21:00.671 --> 00:21:03.760
At the beginning, what will
invariably happen is that,

00:21:03.761 --> 00:21:05.725
you'll forget some of those,

00:21:05.726 --> 00:21:08.920
and hopefully the worst
thing that will happen is

00:21:08.921 --> 00:21:12.500
that you'll get a ticket for
speeding or something like that.

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:15.955
This is illustrating two ways
in which you're learning.

00:21:15.956 --> 00:21:19.525
You're actively maintaining
information and trying to apply it,

00:21:19.526 --> 00:21:21.160
that's working memory, and then,

00:21:21.161 --> 00:21:23.710
you're also getting feedback when you

00:21:23.711 --> 00:21:26.590
mess up or encouragements
if you're doing well,

00:21:26.591 --> 00:21:28.790
and that's reinforcement learning.

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:37.520
I think of them as being at two
different ends of a trade off.

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:42.580
One, learning incremental
integrating information

00:21:42.581 --> 00:21:44.110
in the sense of the value or

00:21:44.111 --> 00:21:46.930
the policy that we're
trying to apply.

00:21:46.931 --> 00:21:49.540
In that sense, it's inflexible,

00:21:49.541 --> 00:21:51.850
but the positive for this is that,

00:21:51.851 --> 00:21:55.090
it's a very broad capacity.

00:21:55.091 --> 00:21:57.190
You can learn lots of things
with reinforcement learning,

00:21:57.191 --> 00:21:58.810
it's robust in the long-term,

00:21:58.811 --> 00:22:02.005
and it's fairly effortless.

00:22:02.006 --> 00:22:04.285
In the other direction,

00:22:04.286 --> 00:22:08.665
working memory is one shot kind
of learning, very fast.

00:22:08.666 --> 00:22:12.760
It stores information very
precisely, and it's flexible.

00:22:12.761 --> 00:22:17.065
We can operate over operations in
working memory over information,

00:22:17.066 --> 00:22:21.385
and the downside is via
its resource or capacity limited.

00:22:21.386 --> 00:22:23.935
Amount of information
you can hold is limited,

00:22:23.936 --> 00:22:27.550
it's limited in time
too, and it's effortful.

00:22:27.551 --> 00:22:33.295
It's something that we have to
engage cognitive attention into.

00:22:33.296 --> 00:22:36.820
What I wanted to do is try to develop

00:22:36.821 --> 00:22:40.765
