01:10:38.630 --> 01:10:43.290
&gt;&gt; Yes. I mean, I can think
of it more in the behavior

01:10:43.291 --> 01:10:47.070
than in the brain side of my work,

01:10:47.071 --> 01:10:50.310
but that would have been
my second part of my talk, is it.

01:10:50.311 --> 01:10:54.390
So, the other half my research is
focused on trying to understand

01:10:54.391 --> 01:10:59.460
how humans learn
more interesting behavior,

01:10:59.461 --> 01:11:08.475
hierarchical behavior and how
this allows us to generalize.

01:11:08.476 --> 01:11:11.115
So, an example, I like to give is,

01:11:11.116 --> 01:11:13.470
I've never been in
this room before and

01:11:13.471 --> 01:11:16.275
despite that I know perfectly
well how to behave in this room.

01:11:16.276 --> 01:11:18.015
It's a conference room,

01:11:18.016 --> 01:11:21.660
I have a whole set of behaviors
that's associated with that,

01:11:21.661 --> 01:11:25.665
that I can reload
immediately and make use of,

01:11:25.666 --> 01:11:27.750
and even if it looked
very different from

01:11:27.751 --> 01:11:30.510
any conference room I had seen
before I would know how to do that.

01:11:30.511 --> 01:11:35.475
So, there's something very high
level about this inference.

01:11:35.476 --> 01:11:41.235
So, part of my work has been to
try to understand how we create

01:11:41.236 --> 01:11:44.835
the structure for learning and

01:11:44.836 --> 01:11:47.400
something very interesting that

01:11:47.401 --> 01:11:49.845
I've been able to show there is that,

01:11:49.846 --> 01:11:53.070
it's really a creation
process rather than

01:11:53.071 --> 01:11:56.985
a discovery process
that participants,

01:11:56.986 --> 01:11:59.490
we were talking about a bit earlier,

01:11:59.491 --> 01:12:03.450
that participants search
for structure and often

01:12:03.451 --> 01:12:05.310
find more structure than there is

01:12:05.311 --> 01:12:08.340
for real and create the structure.

01:12:08.341 --> 01:12:10.500
This is a very costly process

01:12:10.501 --> 01:12:12.240
and behavior actually
that's something

01:12:12.241 --> 01:12:16.140
else I've shown that it has
a cost in how fast we learn,

01:12:16.141 --> 01:12:18.855
how efficiently we
make decisions, etc.,

01:12:18.856 --> 01:12:22.815
but it comes at a very great benefits

01:12:22.816 --> 01:12:26.160
down the line of having created

01:12:26.161 --> 01:12:29.160
representations that are flexible
enough that we can generalize

01:12:29.161 --> 01:12:33.780
them and transfer them.

01:12:33.781 --> 01:12:36.900
Everything you have seen off
generalization and transfer in

01:12:36.901 --> 01:12:40.080
AI has been discovery
rather than creation,

01:12:40.081 --> 01:12:42.900
so I haven't seen, again,

01:12:42.901 --> 01:12:44.400
I might be completely wrong and I

01:12:44.401 --> 01:12:46.815
love to be proven wrong actually.

01:12:46.816 --> 01:12:49.920
But, I haven't seen

01:12:49.921 --> 01:12:56.175
really AI is doing more work for
themselves than they should.

01:12:56.176 --> 01:12:59.340
Like creating more complex
representations than they

01:12:59.341 --> 01:13:04.470
should as a way

01:13:04.471 --> 01:13:09.450
to learn better later

01:13:09.451 --> 01:13:12.540
and that's something that
I've seen not just in adults,

01:13:12.541 --> 01:13:15.795
but I've seen it in
eight- month old infants

01:13:15.796 --> 01:13:19.170
and other people have
seen it in rodents.

01:13:19.171 --> 01:13:26.940
So, it seems like a fairly core
important aspects of learning,

01:13:26.941 --> 01:13:30.720
of dramatization and you
can think of it also as

01:13:30.721 --> 01:13:33.300
exploration because once you have

01:13:33.301 --> 01:13:36.240
those high level kind of strategies,

01:13:36.241 --> 01:13:38.220
instead of exploring at a low level,

01:13:38.221 --> 01:13:40.080
you can explore at

01:13:40.081 --> 01:13:46.050
a more strategic level and
in a more organized way.

01:13:46.051 --> 01:13:49.185
&gt;&gt; Any AI you could normally
have a network with

01:13:49.186 --> 01:13:53.175
larger capacities than required
when it tends to overfit a lot.

01:13:53.176 --> 01:13:55.710
So, I don't know how you can

01:13:55.711 --> 01:13:59.130
actually encourage
exportation by increasing.

01:13:59.131 --> 01:14:03.100
&gt;&gt; I don't know either,
that's your job.

01:14:03.230 --> 01:14:06.000
Yeah, I don't know.

01:14:06.001 --> 01:14:07.560
I've tried to think about it

01:14:07.561 --> 01:14:09.630
and it feels like it
would be really hard.

01:14:09.631 --> 01:14:11.520
Yeah. But, it seems like

01:14:11.521 --> 01:14:14.580
a really important aspect
of in behavior, so yeah.

01:14:14.581 --> 01:14:17.505
&gt;&gt; Since we are working on combining

